# Root-level .dockerignore.
#
# human-reid-service is built with the *repo root* as its build context
# (see surveilance-app-host/AppHost1/Program.cs and the Render deployment),
# so the Dockerfile's "COPY human-reid-service/..." paths resolve the same
# way locally and in production. Without this file, Docker has to hash and
# transfer the ENTIRE repository as build context on every build — including
# multi-GB dataset folders, captured frames, training run artifacts, and
# other services' venv/node_modules directories — none of which the
# human-reid image needs. That is what caused builds to take 5-10+ minutes
# transferring context and occasionally get canceled outright.
#
# Exclude everything by default, then re-allow only what the Dockerfile
# actually copies.
*
!human-reid-service
!human-reid-service/**

# Still exclude noise inside human-reid-service itself.
human-reid-service/venv
human-reid-service/**/__pycache__
human-reid-service/**/*.pyc
human-reid-service/.env
